🌐 Logical Addressing and Address Mapping Techniques
🎯 Objective
To implement IPv4/IPv6 addressing and simulate the operational mechanics of ARP, RARP, BOOTP, and DHCP for address resolution and dynamic allocation.

📘 Theory & Protocol Overview
🆚 IPv4 vs IPv6
Demonstrates 32-bit vs 128-bit addressing and their respective connectivity tests.

🔍 ARP (Address Resolution Protocol)
Resolves a known Logical Address (IP) to a Physical Address (MAC).

⚙️ DHCP (Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol)
Automates IP assignment using the DORA process (Discover, Offer, Request, Acknowledge).

📟 BOOTP
An older protocol for diskless workstations to obtain an IP address from a server.

🖧 Network Topology
Central Infrastructure:

1 Cisco 2911 Router

1 Cisco 2960 Switch

Endpoints:

2 PCs (configured for dual-stack IPv4/IPv6)

Management:

1 Server acting as the DHCP / BOOTP / RARP host

📋 Addressing Table
Device	IPv4 Address	IPv6 Address
PC0	192.168.1.2	2001:db8::1/64
PC1	192.168.1.3	2001:db8::2/64
Server	192.168.1.10	2001:db8::10/64
